/* history.js — each continent's story, from about 5000 BCE (earlier where the
   story starts earlier) to today. Bizzing India's Itihaas is the model: a
   river of ages, each with a hook, the story, what happened step by step,
   the places you can still stand in, and how we know.

   EDITORIAL (Bizzing India docs/05, which binds the family):
   · Dates are approximate and SAY so. No false precision.
   · Empires are drawn as SOFT ZONES OF INFLUENCE — blurred, named, never a
     line. Real edges faded, moved and were argued over. Modern borders appear
     only in each continent's last age, "today".
   · Rulers are people, not teams; everyday life and ideas beat battles.
   · Hard history (conquest, slavery, colonial rule, world wars) is told
     plainly and gently, never graphically. `hard` on a moment hides it below
     the 11–14 band; the age says there is more for older explorers.
   · Every age names where it is checked (`src`), and the whole shelf awaits
     a second reader (HISTORY_NEEDS_REVIEW) — the screen says so.

   zones: [lat, lng, radius km, name]   sites: [name, lat, lng, one line]
   `paint` is the plate prompt: a PLACE of that age, no people, no lettering. */

